# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-addon-sqd` package. We use sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) to refine noisy samples taken from a quantum circuit that approximates the ground state of a chemistry Hamiltonian. Ground state energies are approximated by diagonalizing the Hamiltonian in subspaces formed by the refined samples.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng gabay na ito ang isang minimal na gumaganang halimbawa ng package na `qiskit-addon-sqd`. Gumagamit tayo ng sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) para pinuhin ang mga maingay na sample na kinuha mula sa isang quantum circuit na tumatantiya sa ground state ng isang chemistry Hamiltonian. Tinatantiya ang mga ground state energy sa pamamagitan ng pag-diagonalize sa Hamiltonian sa mga subspace na binuo ng mga pinong sample.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more explanatory end-to-end workflows that run on quantum hardware, check out the tutorials:\n"
msgstr "Para sa mas detalyadong end-to-end na mga workflow na tumatakbo sa quantum hardware, tingnan ang mga tutorial:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Sample-based quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization): chemistry Hamiltonian workflow\n"
msgstr "[Sample-based quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization): workflow ng chemistry Hamiltonian\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization): fermionic lattice model workflow\n"
msgstr "[Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization): workflow ng fermionic lattice model\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the inputs for SQD {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-sqd}"
msgstr "1. Ihanda ang mga input para sa SQD {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we define the chemistry Hamiltonian and quantum circuit that approximates its ground state. The system studied in this example is N₂ at equilibrium geometry in STO-3G basis with two core orbitals frozen. This system has ``8`` spatial orbitals and ``10`` electrons, which means the quantum circuit is defined on ``16`` qubits, where qubits ``0-7`` represent spin-up orbitals and qubits ``8-15`` represent spin-down orbitals. Since this is a closed-shell system with ``10`` electrons, we know each physically-valid sample should have hamming weight ``10``, where the hamming weight of both the left and right halves of the bitstring is ``5``.\n"
msgstr "Una, tinutukoy natin ang chemistry Hamiltonian at ang quantum circuit na tumatantiya sa ground state nito. Ang sistemang pinag-aaralan sa halimbawang ito ay N₂ sa equilibrium geometry sa STO-3G basis na may dalawang frozen na core orbital. May ``8`` spatial orbital at ``10`` electron ang sistemang ito, kaya ang quantum circuit ay nakadefine sa ``16`` qubit, kung saan ang mga qubit na ``0-7`` ay kumakatawan sa mga spin-up orbital at ang mga qubit na ``8-15`` ay kumakatawan sa mga spin-down orbital. Dahil closed-shell ang sistemang ito na may ``10`` electron, alam nating ang bawat physically-valid na sample ay dapat may hamming weight na ``10``, kung saan ang hamming weight ng kaliwa at kanang kalahati ng bitstring ay ``5``.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Generate noisy samples {#2-generate-noisy-samples}"
msgstr "2. Gumawa ng mga maingay na sample {#2-generate-noisy-samples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a real workflow you would design an ansatz circuit, optimize it for hardware, and sample it on the QPU. Here we skip that and draw ``10,000`` uniformly random bitstrings instead. While our samples contain no information about the actual ground state, we will see that the SQD protocol can still recover the true ground state by iteratively refining these samples, diagonalizing, and using the energies at each iteration to inform the next round of bitstring refinement. We can eventually recover the exact ground state in this manner because the subspace containing the ground state is small enough to calculate exactly. Specifically, since we know each half of each bitstring (``8`` bits) should have hamming weight ``5``, we know the full Hilbert subspace of the system is size $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$.\n"
msgstr "Sa totoong workflow, magdidisenyo ka ng ansatz circuit, i-o-optimize ito para sa hardware, at kukuha ng sample mula rito sa QPU. Dito, lalaktawan natin iyon at gagawa na lang tayo ng ``10,000`` na uniformly random na mga bitstring. Kahit walang impormasyon ang mga sample natin tungkol sa totoong ground state, makikita nating mababawi pa rin ng SQD protocol ang tunay na ground state sa pamamagitan ng paulit-ulit na pagpino sa mga sample na ito, pag-diagonalize, at paggamit sa mga energy sa bawat iteration para gabayan ang susunod na round ng pagpino ng bitstring. Mababawi natin sa wakas ang eksaktong ground state sa ganitong paraan dahil sapat na maliit ang subspace na naglalaman ng ground state para makalkula nang eksakto. Partikular, dahil alam nating ang bawat kalahati ng bawat bitstring (``8`` bit) ay dapat may hamming weight na ``5``, alam nating ang buong Hilbert subspace ng sistema ay may sukat na $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Post-process with SQD {#3-post-process-with-sqd}"
msgstr "3. I-post-process gamit ang SQD {#3-post-process-with-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The objective of the SQD algorithm is to refine noisy samples taken from a QPU and ultimately diagonalize the Hamiltonian in a subspace spanned by those refined samples. This is done iteratively as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang layunin ng SQD algorithm ay pinuhin ang mga maingay na sample na kinuha mula sa isang QPU at sa huli ay i-diagonalize ang Hamiltonian sa isang subspace na binuo ng mga pinong sample na iyon. Paulit-ulit itong ginagawa ayon sa sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refine samples by postselecting only those which have correct particle number for both the spin-up and spin-down subsystems\n"
msgstr "Pinuhin ang mga sample sa pamamagitan ng pag-postselect lamang ng mga may tamang particle number para sa parehong spin-up at spin-down na subsystem\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonalize in small subspaces spanned by the refined samples and collect information about the subspaces that yield the the best (lowest) energies.\n"
msgstr "I-diagonalize sa maliliit na subspace na binuo ng mga pinong sample at mangolekta ng impormasyon tungkol sa mga subspace na nagbibigay ng pinakamahusay (pinakamababang) energy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each iteration:\n"
msgstr "Sa bawat iteration:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refine the noisy samples by probabilistically flipping bits in samples with incorrect particle number. The probabilities are calculated using the subspace information from the most recent diagonalization.\n"
msgstr "Pinuhin ang mga maingay na sample sa pamamagitan ng probabilistikong pag-flip ng mga bit sa mga sample na may maling particle number. Kinakalkula ang mga probability gamit ang impormasyon ng subspace mula sa pinakahuling diagonalization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonalize in small subspaces spanned by the refined samples\n"
msgstr "I-diagonalize sa maliliit na subspace na binuo ng mga pinong sample\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collect information about the subspaces yielding the best (lowest) energies\n"
msgstr "Mangolekta ng impormasyon tungkol sa mga subspace na nagbibigay ng pinakamahusay (pinakamababang) energy\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can see from the output that the algorithm converges to the exact ground state energy after ``6`` iterations and that the diagonalization is performed over the full Hilbert subspace of dimension $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$. Of course, diagonalizing over the full subspace is usually not feasible, and therefore, systems with ground states having sparse support are the most likely to benefit from subspace diagonalization techniques such as SQD.\n"
msgstr "Makikita natin sa output na nagko-converge ang algorithm sa eksaktong ground state energy pagkatapos ng ``6`` iteration at ang diagonalization ay ginagawa sa buong Hilbert subspace na may dimensyon na $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$. Siyempre, kadalasan ay hindi praktikal ang pag-diagonalize sa buong subspace, kaya ang mga sistemang may ground state na may sparse na suporta ang pinakamalamang na makinabang sa mga subspace diagonalization technique tulad ng SQD.\n"

